==Trivia==
*Snache's name may be derived from ''snake'' and ''ache'', ''blanche'' (French for white), ''[[wikipedia:Gouache|gouache]]'' (an opaque watercolor paint containing a white filler) or ''panache'' (a flamboyant and stylish way of doing things).
*Snache is shaped like its Japanese namesake, ''Nyoro'' (にょろ), another name for a wave dash (〜) or tilde (~). In fact, a tilde appears depending on which version of Romaji is used to transliterate this Japanese name.
*Snache has no stated gender in [[The Battle Cats]], but was referred to as male in its description from the first English version, [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|Battle Cats]]: "He uses water colors for body painting. So, he hates water. This info has nothing to do with the game content."
*Snache and most of its variants possess fourth-wall-breaking descriptions with emphasis on their use of watercolor paint or possible weakness to water attacks. However, only [[Metal Snache]], an event enemy with no description, is actually weak to [[Ototo Corps#Waterblast|water]].
*The Japanese descriptions of Snache and all its non-event variants describe their shapes. Snache and [[Sinner Snache]] are snakes shaped like snakes, [[Ginger Snache]] is a snake shaped like a Snache, and [[Znache]] is a creature that is shaped like a Snache and can be mistaken for a [[wikipedia:Tsuchinoko|tsuchinoko]], but is academically closer to an earthworm.
*In [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]], [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A5%DF%A5%A4%A5%E9%C3%CB Miira-Otoko] (ミイラ男, "Mummy Man") had a similar description to Snache, explaining how his extreme dryness makes him weak to fire, only to then point out that the game doesn't have a fire trait.
**Later, the game would receive a fire-related trait, [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/%A4%C7%A4%B9 Death], and a Death Miira-Otoko variant: [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A5%C7%A5%A3%A5%A8%A5%B9%A1%A6%A5%DF%A5%A3%A5%E9%A5%A8 Dies Miirae] (ディエス・ミィラエ), anxious and stressed about the addition of a fire trait to the game and unaware that it hasn't actually had much of an effect on him.

